19:T5b1,## Intent

Sometimes constructing an object is **expensive**, it parses a file, hits a database, runs a heavy computation, or the exact concrete class **isn't known** at compile time. Prototype sidesteps both: keep one ready-made instance around and **copy it** whenever you need another.

## How it works

Every prototype implements a single method:

```
interface Shape {
    Shape clone();          // each shape copies itself
}
```

Asking an object to clone itself returns a new object of the **same concrete type** with the same field values, no `new Circle()` followed by re-setting radius and color by hand.

## Shallow vs deep copy

The one thing that bites people. A **shallow** clone copies the top-level fields; if a field is a reference (a list, a nested object), the copy and the original end up **pointing at the same thing**:

- **Shallow copy**, referenced objects are *shared*; mutating the copy's list mutates the original's too. 💥
- **Deep copy**, referenced objects are *also cloned*, so the copy is fully **independent**. ✓

## Registry

A prototype **registry** stores pre-built, named templates (`"red-circle"`, `"dashed-rect"`). Callers `registry.get("red-circle").clone()` instead of remembering how to configure one from scratch, the registry hands back a fresh, ready-to-use copy.

> Contrast with `new` + manual re-configuration: with Prototype the *configured state travels with the object*, so you never repeat the setup.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-creational","activeLesson":"prototype"}],["$","$L18","prototype",{"lesson":{"id":"prototype","patternId":"lld-creational","title":"Prototype","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Create new objects by CLONING an existing, fully-configured instance, instead of building from scratch with `new`.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Adobe"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Clone, don't rebuild","code":["interface Shape {","    Shape clone();                 // every shape can copy itself","}","class Circle implements Shape {","    int radius; Color color;","    public Shape clone() {","        return new Circle(radius, color);   // same field values","    }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"Shape declares one method: clone(). Every shape promises it can produce a copy of itself.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"proto","name":"Shape","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ clone(): Shape"],"x":1,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"circle","name":"Circle","fields":["- radius","- color"],"methods":["+ clone()"],"x":0.4,"y":1.5},{"id":"rect","name":"Rectangle","fields":["- w, h"],"methods":["+ clone()"],"x":1.7,"y":1.5}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"circle","to":"proto","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r2","from":"rect","to":"proto","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["proto"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["proto"]},"vars":[["contract","clone(): Shape"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":6,"narration":"Circle and Rectangle implement clone(), each returning a NEW instance of its own type carrying the same field values.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["proto","circle","rect"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2"],"activeIds":["circle","rect"]},"vars":[["each clone","returns same type"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":7,"narration":"Instead of `new Circle()` and then re-setting radius and color by hand, you copy a template that's already configured, the state comes along for free.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["proto","circle","rect"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2"],"activeIds":["circle"]},"vars":[["vs new","no re-config"]]}]},{"label":"An independent copy","code":["Circle original = configuredRedCircle();   // expensive to set up","Circle copy = (Circle) original.clone();   // cheap: just copy it","copy.color = BLUE;                          // change the copy…","assert original.color == RED;              // …original untouched"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"The Client calls clone() on a fully-configured original, no need to know how it was built.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"c","label":"Client","kind":"actor"},{"id":"o","label":"original","tint":"accent"},{"id":"cp","label":"copy"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"c","to":"o","label":"clone()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"o","to":"cp","label":"copy of self","kind":"create"},{"id":"m3","from":"o","to":"c","label":"the copy","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0},"vars":[["original","already configured"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"clone() creates a NEW object copying the original's state. With a deep copy, any nested lists or objects are copied too, not shared.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":2,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["watch","shallow share 💥"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"The Client gets back an independent copy. Change the copy's color and the original is untouched, that's the deep-copy guarantee.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":2},"vars":[["copy","independent of original ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
